  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 126 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe aforementioned upper level ridge begins to build over the\nregion on Monday allowing mid-level heights to begin to rise.\nThis will lead to sunny conditions and daytime heating bringing\nhighs in the mid/upper 80s to low 90s on Monday, and into the\nupper 80s to mid 90s Tuesday (both days showing the warmer end\nof that range west of Highway 65). \n\nAn upper level low over Canada will push a shortwave trough \nthrough the Northern Plains during the beginning of the week. \nGuidance suggests the associated upper level energy sliding into\nour forecast area by Wednesday night, bringing additional \nchances (20-40%) for showers and storms, primarily north of \nHighway 60. As this is still several days out, we'll have to \njust keep an eye on how models handle this system to see what \nit'll be capable of. \n\nLooking ahead towards the 8-14 Day timeframe, CPC is showcasing\na Moderate Risk for extreme heat as we head towards the middle\nof the month, so make sure to enjoy this brief reprieve from \nthe heat before temperatures start climbing back above normal!",
